{
  "format": "playground-scenario",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Stage 1 gate: a generated town lives on its own for two weeks and keeps its social history",
  "description": "A seeded 14-resident town made by the generator, with only the base game loaded through the pack loader, runs 14 game days on its own. Every day is re-simulated from its snapshot on another thread count and must agree. The town must have a past (relationships, memories, remembered conversations, journal entries); a save and reload gives the identical state, so that past is intact; a run resumed from a snapshot agrees; and damage to the newest save falls back to the older one with the past still there.",
